{
  "id": "tot-phenomenon",
  "term": "TOT phenomenon",
  "definition": "The TOT phenomenon, or tip-of-the-tongue phenomenon, is a common word-finding problem in which a person strongly feels they know a word, especially a name, but cannot retrieve it at that moment. It is described as a failure to access the word’s sound form rather than a loss of its meaning, and it tends to occur more often with increasing age.",
